# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What stays OUT of git, and why. Check a file with:  git check-ignore -v <path>
# Rule of thumb: if it can be rebuilt, is private to your machine, or is a secret,
# it does not belong in the repository.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. SECRETS: the most important section ───────────────────────────────────
# Real values (database password, JWT secret, API keys) live in .env, which must
# never be committed. A secret pushed to GitHub is compromised even if deleted later.
# .env.example is the opposite: placeholders only, committed so newcomers know which
# variables exist.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Private keys and certificates (SSH, TLS, signing keys).
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
# Cloud and service credentials.
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ── 2. BUILD OUTPUT: rebuilt by `npm run build` ──────────────────────────────
/dist
/build
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── 3. DEPENDENCIES: restored by `npm install` ───────────────────────────────
/node_modules

# ── 4. GENERATED CODE: rebuilt by `npm install` / `npm run db:generate` ──────
# The Prisma client is generated from prisma/schema.prisma. Committing it would
# create noisy diffs and stale copies. (prisma/migrations/ IS committed: it is the
# history of the database.)
/src/generated

# ── 5. TEST AND DIAGNOSTIC OUTPUT ────────────────────────────────────────────
/coverage
/.nyc_output
# Node diagnostic reports.
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json

# ── 6. LOGS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs can contain request ids, emails and IPs: never commit them.
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ── 7. LOCAL DATA AND SCRATCH FILES ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Database dumps and local data can contain real personal information.
*.sql.gz
*.dump
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Temporary and backup files.
.temp
.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.swp
# Process ids and runtime data.
pids
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock

# ── 8. EDITORS AND TOOLS: personal preferences, not project files ────────────
# Ignored entirely, so a stray editor setting is never published by accident.
# To share editor settings with a team, replace the first line with `.vscode/*` and
# add `!.vscode/settings.json` (and tasks/launch/extensions) underneath.
.vscode/
/.idea
.project
.classpath
.c9/
*.launch
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace
# Claude Code: personal permissions and local settings.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# ── 9. OPERATING SYSTEM FILES ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
